      "Treat the control as a queue item with an owner, a due time, and a close condition. A task that has no close condition becomes an open loop that survives the week. At the Outsourced Billing Services review, the billing manager compares this step with the claim file and denial appeal record before closing it.",
      "Do not copy a value from a prior record for the claim file because it looks familiar. Reopen the source, confirm the version, and record what changed. In outsourced medical billing operations, the claim file and denial appeal evidence stays with the case so the billing manager can verify what changed.",
